@startuml
title Crash Recovery - Worker Dies During Task 2

participant "RabbitMQ" as RMQ
participant "Celery Worker" as Worker
database "PostgreSQL" as DB
participant "Tools" as Tools

== Task 2 is executing ==
RMQ -> Worker: deliver collect_deployments message
Worker -> DB: query step status (idempotency check)
DB --> Worker: status = RUNNING (not yet SUCCEEDED)
Worker -> Worker: begin executing collect_deployments tool
Worker -> Tools: execute collect_deployments()

note over Worker: WORKER CRASHES HERE

== RabbitMQ detects failure ==
note over RMQ: connection drops, message unacked
note over RMQ: message re-queued for redelivery

== Worker restarts ==
note over Worker: new worker process starts, reconnects to RMQ

RMQ -> Worker: redeliver collect_deployments message

== Task 2 resumes (idempotent replay) ==
Worker -> DB: query step status (idempotency check)

alt step status = SUCCEEDED (completed before crash)
    Worker -> RMQ: publish retrieve_runbooks (Task 3)
    Worker -> RMQ: ack
else step status = RUNNING (crash happened mid-execution)
    Worker -> DB: read Task 1 result from Postgres
    DB --> Worker: Task 1 result (logs data)
    Worker -> Tools: execute collect_deployments (again)
    Tools --> Worker: deployment data
    Worker -> DB: UPDATE step status=SUCCEEDED, result=<deployments>
    Worker -> RMQ: publish retrieve_runbooks (Task 3)
    Worker -> RMQ: ack
end

== Workflow continues normally ==
note over RMQ: Task 3 message in queue
note over Worker: picks up Task 3, continues workflow

@enduml